1. I think that `__builtin_*` should be prioritized over `_BitScanForward*` - it's possible to use compilers on Windows that have those built-ins.
2. In general, you should avoid creating functions and variables with leading underscores because they are reserved to the compiler.
3. I believe that this procedure should always be a static function instead of either a function or a macro.

```suggestion
static int pandas_ctzll(unsigned long long mask) {
#if __has_builtin(__builtin_ctzll)
return __builtin_ctzll(mask);
#elif defined(_MSC_VER)
  unsigned long index;
  _BitScanForward64(&index, mask);
  return (int)index;
#else
#error ctz required
#endif
}
```

Probably will have to [define a `__has_builtin` macro](https://releases.llvm.org/5.0.1/tools/clang/docs/LanguageExtensions.html#has-builtin) too.

